.TH CREDSCOPE 1 "2026-07-27" "credscope" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
credscope \- analyze static credential exposure and reachability
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B credscope
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B credscope
is an experimental, offline\-first command\-line tool for analyzing static
credential exposure and reachability context in Docker Compose files,
GitHub Actions workflows, and imported Gitleaks JSON reports. It builds a
typed graph of credentials, permissions, ports, mounts, dependencies, and
shared network topology, then scores and reports the findings.
.PP
.B credscope
performs deterministic static analysis only. It does not validate whether
discovered credentials are active, execute repository content, workflows,
or containers, or make network requests. It is not a complete
vulnerability scanner, is not a replacement for Gitleaks or another
secret scanner, and its findings should not be the sole basis for a
security decision.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B credscope version
Print the tool version, commit, and build date, then exit.
.TP
.BI "credscope scan " [repository]
Analyze the repository at
.I repository
(default: the current directory) and produce a report. See
.B SCAN OPTIONS
below.
.TP
.B credscope rules list
List every stable rule identifier (for example
.BR CRD101 )
and its short title, one per line, sorted by identifier.
.TP
.BI "credscope explain " RULE_ID
Print the full title for a stable rule identifier, for example
.BR "credscope explain CRD101" .
.SH SCAN OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "\-\-gitleaks\-report " path
Path to an imported Gitleaks JSON report. Raw
.B Secret
and
.B Match
values from the report are fingerprinted and discarded; they are never
written to a credscope report.
.TP
.BI "\-\-gitleaks\-path\-prefix " prefix
Exact absolute scanner path prefix to strip from Gitleaks finding paths
(for reports generated inside a container).
.TP
.BI "\-\-profile " profile
Environment profile:
.BR auto ", " local ", " ci ", " staging ", or " production .
.TP
.BI "\-\-format " format ", \-f " format
Report format. See
.B REPORT FORMATS
below. Default:
.BR terminal .
.TP
.BI "\-\-output " path ", \-o " path
Write the report to
.I path
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BI "\-\-fail\-on " severity
Failure threshold:
.BR none ", " informational ", " low ", " medium ", " high ", or " critical .
Default:
.BR none .
.TP
.BI "\-\-minimum\-score " score
Minimum risk score (0\-100) to report.
.TP
.BI "\-\-include " pattern
Additional repository\-relative include pattern. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI "\-\-exclude " pattern
Repository\-relative exclude pattern. May be repeated.
.TP
.BI "\-\-config " path
Configuration file. Defaults to
.B .credscope.yml
in the repository root when present.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Disable colored terminal output.
.TP
.B \-\-quiet ", \-q"
Suppress non\-result output.
.TP
.B \-\-verbose ", \-v"
Show detailed, secret\-safe evidence.
.SH REPORT FORMATS
.TP
.B terminal
Human\-readable, optionally colored, sanitized terminal output.
.TP
.B html
A standalone, offline HTML report with no external scripts, styles,
fonts, or network requests.
.TP
.B json
Deterministic, machine\-readable JSON (schema version 2).
.TP
.B sarif
SARIF 2.1.0, suitable for GitHub code scanning and other SARIF consumers.
.TP
.B mermaid
A Mermaid flowchart of the typed credential/reachability graph, embedded
in a fenced Markdown code block.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success; no configured risk threshold was exceeded.
.TP
.B 1
The scan completed but the configured
.B \-\-fail\-on
/
.B \-\-minimum\-score
threshold was exceeded.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (invalid flags, invalid configuration).
.TP
.B 3
Malformed input (an unreadable or invalid discovered file, Gitleaks
report, or path).
.TP
.B 4
Internal error (for example, a report could not be written).
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Print the version:
.PP
.RS
credscope version
.RE
.PP
Scan the current repository and print a terminal report:
.PP
.RS
credscope scan .
.RE
.PP
Scan a repository, importing a Gitleaks report, and write an HTML report:
.PP
.RS
credscope scan . \-\-gitleaks\-report gitleaks.json \-\-format html \-\-output credscope\-report.html
.RE
.PP
List every stable rule identifier:
.PP
.RS
credscope rules list
.RE
.SH SECURITY MODEL
.B credscope
does not validate whether credentials are active, execute repository
content, workflows, or containers, make network requests, or prove
runtime data flow or external network exposure. Repository discovery,
imported reports, configuration, and output writes remain confined to
the selected repository root.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation, the rule catalog, and the scoring policy are
installed under
.IR /usr/share/doc/credscope/ .
